
                                                   CHECK COMMAND


Checks for data of type IHEX, ASCII or reference data at a particular address.

Below is the syntax :
                 check 	-t {"IHEX"|"ASCII"|"REF"}  -addr address  -val value  [-l len]  [-n name] 

---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES       |    DESCRIPTION
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -t          |    Specifies type IHEX, REF or ASCII. Mandatory switch.
   -addr       |    Address at which the data is checked. Mandatory switch.
   -val        |    Specifies the value to be checked. If the type is REF, value at address specified in -val is
               |    considered for comparison. Mandatory switch.
   -l          |    For type IHEX and ASCII, length switch is an optional. If the type is REF then -l is a mandatory
               |    switch.
   -n          |    Specifies the name of the command. Optional.
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Example:
	read -in medc18.hex -igCks true	
	check -t IHEX -addr 0x80030010 -val 0x123456
	check -t REF -addr 0x80040020 -val 0x80020010 -l 0x20
	check -t ASCII -addr 0x80030010 -val 12345678 -n "Check Data"
	write -out output.hex -lyt 0x10
	
